7. Why Do We Return Only root.val + max(left,right)?

This is perhaps the most important concept in the problem.

Suppose:

        10
       /  \
      5    8

At node 10, the best complete path can be:

5 → 10 → 8

So:

pathsum = 5 + 10 + 8
        = 23

But if 10 has a parent:

          20
         /
        10
       /  \
      5    8

The path returned to 20 cannot be:

20 → 10 → 5
       ↘ 8

because that branches.

It must choose one side:

20 → 10 → 5

or:

20 → 10 → 8

Therefore:

return root.val + max(left,right)

while the global answer can use:

left + root.val + right
8. Two Different Values at Every Node

This is the key to understanding the entire problem.

At each node we calculate:

A. Complete path through current node
left + root.val + right

This can use both children.

We use it to update:

ans
B. Gain returned to parent
root.val + max(left,right)

This can use only one child.

We return it from helper().

So:

             Current Node
                  |
       ┌──────────┴──────────┐
       ↓                     ↓
 Complete Path          One-side Gain
       ↓                     ↓
left + root + right   root + max(left,right)
       ↓                     ↓
   update ans          return to parent

This is the fundamental Tree DP idea.

