12. Your Final Optimal Code

This is your code with slightly clearer variable names:

class Solution {

    int ans = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

    public int maxPathSum(TreeNode root) {
        helper(root);
        return ans;
    }

    int helper(TreeNode root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return 0;
        }

        // Maximum useful contribution from left subtree
        int leftGain = Math.max(helper(root.left), 0);

        // Maximum useful contribution from right subtree
        int rightGain = Math.max(helper(root.right), 0);

        // Complete path passing through current node
        int pathSum = root.val + leftGain + rightGain;

        // Update global answer
        ans = Math.max(ans, pathSum);

        // Return only one branch to parent
        return root.val + Math.max(leftGain, rightGain);
    }
}
🧠 13. Interview Pattern

This problem and 543 Diameter of Binary Tree have almost the same structure.

543 — Diameter
left height
right height

answer = left + right

return 1 + max(left,right)
124 — Maximum Path Sum
left gain
right gain

answer = left + root.val + right

return root.val + max(left,right)

So the reusable pattern is:

              Postorder DFS
                   |
          ┌────────┴────────┐
          ↓                 ↓
      left result       right result
          |                 |
          └────────┬────────┘
                   ↓
            calculate answer
                   ↓
            return to parent
